  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0 — the standards release.\n\n* AddArkOidcClient now configures ASP.NET Core's OpenID Connect and cookie handlers against the\n  provider's discovery document. Real PKCE, state and nonce validation, JWKS rollover and silent\n  refresh all come from the framework instead of being hand-rolled.\n* Authority and ClientId are the only required settings — no pasted rsaPublic, no issuer/audience\n  to mirror, no per-tenant key table to keep in step with rotation.\n* AddArkOidcApi for protecting an API with bearer tokens from the same provider.\n* Ark authorization claims (ark_claims) are projected onto the principal as role claims, so\n  [Authorize(Roles = \"...\")] and policies work directly.\n* GetArkAccessTokenAsync / WithArkTokenAsync read the current token per call, so a token refreshed\n  by the cookie handler is picked up automatically.\n* New services for the non-interactive flows: ArkSetupProbe (configuration vs. live metadata),\n  ArkClientCredentials (client credentials grant with caching) and ArkRegistration (RFC 7591/7592).\n\nBreaking / migration: the standard flow is now the default. Set ark_oauth_client:UseLegacyFlow to\ntrue to keep the original cookie/bearer middleware while migrating — it does not validate state or\nnonce and should be treated as a migration aid, not a supported configuration.\n\nPackaging: the package no longer ships a sample appsettings file into consuming projects, and now\ncarries a readme, an SPDX license expression and a symbol package.",
